# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# PR Review Tree: local data, worktrees and test artifacts
/slash
/slash-bin
.claude/scripts/server.log
data/*.db
data/*.db-*
# Per-reviewer local settings (who "I" am for @mention detection, see
# settings.go). One person's identity, so never committed — the template
# data/settings.example.json is.
data/settings.json
# Per-reviewer praise-word list (praisewords.go) — personal vocabulary, never
# committed, same reasoning as settings.json above.
data/praise-words.json
# Per-reviewer Jira-notification filter list (notifyfilters.go) — his own noise
# filter, never committed, same reasoning as settings.json above.
data/notify-filters.json
# Per-reviewer debug-mode recording (debug_log.go) — one reviewer's own
# navigation/click history, only exists while Debug mode is on, same reasoning
# as the two files above.
data/debug-log.jsonl
data/worktrees/
data/workflows/
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/
tests/.tmp/

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Local scratch notes
/todo/
